# capture.py regenerates everything below from its own deterministic rasters
# and the vips binary, so only capture.py, commands.sh, oracle.json and the
# JPEG fixtures are pinned.
#
# fixtures/uhdr.jpg is the anchor and cannot be regenerated exactly on a
# machine with a different libultrahdr: the version string libuhdr stamps into
# the gainmap's COM segment goes into the file. Every other JPEG under
# fixtures/ is cut from it, or from fixtures/plain.jpg, by capture.py.
#
# outputs/ holds the .v intermediates, including the 64x64 scRGB source, the
# synthetic gainmap-carrying probes vipsedit builds, and every uhdr2scRGB
# result. It runs to about 100 MB.
fixtures/*.raw
outputs/
